## 2. Counting a tesseract, and hearing the shape of a sphere

A tesseract has face vector $(16, 32, 24, 8, 1)$. Take the alternating sum and you get the Euler characteristic: $1$ for the solid body, and $16-32+24-8=0$ for its boundary 3-sphere. That zero is the combinatorial fingerprint of an odd-dimensional sphere. Explore the pattern for any dimension:

