{{visualization:0}}

## 3. The most beautiful map in mathematics

The Hopf map $(z,w)\mapsto(2z\bar w, |z|^2-|w|^2)$ weaves the 3-sphere out of circles, one for every point of an ordinary 2-sphere. No two circles meet, yet every pair is linked. Pick a base point and watch its fibre appear:

